WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.826
Interval and ratio variables can look similar
because both are numeric and support meaningful
differences

00:00:07.571 --> 00:00:13.219
The major distinction is the zero point Celsius zero
is a reference

00:00:13.245 --> 00:00:18.909
point not the absence of temperature Zero visits
means no visits

00:00:18.922 --> 00:00:24.612
occurred That difference determines whether ratio
statements are meaningful

00:00:26.354 --> 00:00:31.630
When classifying a numeric variable ask what zero
means in the real-world measurement process
